Repair the custom gradient stop editor

A stop carries a position, a value and an alpha. The editor of the
Custom Gradients page loses two of the three on each edit.
itemChanged() reads one other column into a single number. It gives
that number to both untouched components, so an edit of the value cell
also writes the alpha. The same slot erases the old stop with the
percentage of the cell, while the set holds fractions. The erase
therefore misses, and each edit adds a row. updateGradStop() writes
the three cells with the tree signals live, which re-enters
itemChanged() with a stale previous value and adds a fourth stop. That
slot also dereferences the result of find() with no test against
end().

Carry all three components through the edit, and convert the percentage
once. Block the tree signals around each write, and guard the lookup.

Two neighbours of the editor follow. The border list stays enabled for
a gradient that holds no stop, where borderChanged() drops the choice,
so the list now follows the entry. The preview draws the stops of the
dialog, while the writer saves the result of fix(). The two now use
one stop set.

The change sits on the branch work/dialog-state of the local tree, as commit 4 of 12.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

